1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,838
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:02,838 --> 00:00:05,886
It's essential daily conversation practice!

3
00:00:05,886 --> 00:00:09,154
Shall I warm it up?

4
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Ordering Conversation Practice

5
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:14,608
Excuse me.

6
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:18,137
Yes, welcome!

7
00:00:18,161 --> 00:00:22,073
Please take a seat over here.

8
00:00:22,096 --> 00:00:25,066
Thank you.

9
00:00:25,089 --> 00:00:29,478
Could I order, please?

10
00:00:29,501 --> 00:00:34,035
Yes, please go ahead with your order.

11
00:00:34,058 --> 00:00:36,924
What would you like?

12
00:00:36,947 --> 00:00:41,614
What's your recommended dish?

13
00:00:41,637 --> 00:00:48,674
Today's grilled salmon set meal and fried chicken set meal are popular!

14
00:00:48,698 --> 00:00:53,365
What kind of fish is the grilled salmon?

15
00:00:53,388 --> 00:00:58,491
It's grilled salmon with salt today.

16
00:00:58,514 --> 00:01:01,548
It's very delicious.

17
00:01:01,571 --> 00:01:06,037
Salmon, huh? Sounds good!

18
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:10,497
What's included in the fried chicken set meal?

19
00:01:10,521 --> 00:01:15,703
It comes with five pieces of fried chicken.

20
00:01:15,726 --> 00:01:20,993
And it includes salad, rice, and miso soup.

21
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:24,449
That's a lot!

22
00:01:24,472 --> 00:01:29,857
I love meat, so I'll go with the fried chicken set meal.

23
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:32,947
Thank you.

24
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:37,313
How would you like your rice portion?

25
00:01:37,336 --> 00:01:41,473
What sizes do you have?

26
00:01:41,497 --> 00:01:47,397
We have small, regular, and large portions.

27
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:50,887
Large portions are free too.

28
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:54,468
Free?

29
00:01:54,492 --> 00:01:59,458
But I'll have the regular size, please.

30
00:01:59,481 --> 00:02:02,591
Got it.

31
00:02:02,615 --> 00:02:05,715
Regular size it is.

32
00:02:05,738 --> 00:02:10,638
What's in the miso soup?

33
00:02:10,661 --> 00:02:15,361
It has tofu and seaweed in it.

34
00:02:15,384 --> 00:02:19,537
Is there anything spicy in it?

35
00:02:19,561 --> 00:02:24,478
No, there's nothing spicy in it.

36
00:02:24,501 --> 00:02:27,659
You can rest assured!

37
00:02:27,682 --> 00:02:30,635
That's a relief.

38
00:02:30,658 --> 00:02:34,726
What drinks do you have?

39
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:40,138
We have cold water and hot tea.

40
00:02:40,161 --> 00:02:44,670
Then, I'll have hot tea, please.

41
00:02:44,693 --> 00:02:48,006
Understood.

42
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:50,747
Hot tea, coming right up.

43
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:55,239
How long until the food arrives?

44
00:02:55,263 --> 00:02:59,251
It'll be ready in about 10 minutes.

45
00:02:59,274 --> 00:03:01,908
Got it.

46
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:05,797
I'll look forward to it!

47
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:10,495
Let me confirm your order.

48
00:03:10,519 --> 00:03:15,104
Fried chicken set meal (regular size) and hot tea, correct?

49
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:18,923
Yes, that's right.

50
00:03:18,946 --> 00:03:21,902
Thank you for your order.

51
00:03:21,926 --> 00:03:24,916
Thank you.

52
00:03:24,939 --> 00:03:28,707
Please wait a moment.

53
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:30,230
Scene 2: Introduction to Conveyor Belt Sushi

54
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:37,064
Mr. Takeshi, this is my first time at a conveyor belt sushi restaurant.

55
00:03:37,087 --> 00:03:40,023
Really?!

56
00:03:40,046 --> 00:03:45,912
There are so many delicious sushi plates going around here!

57
00:03:45,935 --> 00:03:52,202
The plates are moving—it’s so fun!

58
00:03:52,225 --> 00:03:57,603
First, let’s make some hot tea.

59
00:03:57,626 --> 00:04:01,926
How do I make the tea?

60
00:04:01,949 --> 00:04:10,016
Put this green tea powder in the cup and press that hot water button over there.

61
00:04:10,039 --> 00:04:13,178
Got it.

62
00:04:13,202 --> 00:04:18,778
It dispenses hot water, so be careful!

63
00:04:18,801 --> 00:04:24,906
Okay. Can I grab the plates that are going around?

64
00:04:24,929 --> 00:04:29,231
You can also order using the touchscreen.

65
00:04:29,255 --> 00:04:34,793
Oh, so I can order from the touchscreen too?

66
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:37,892
That’s convenient!

67
00:04:37,915 --> 00:04:42,581
An-san, what kind of fish do you like?

68
00:04:42,604 --> 00:04:48,071
I love salmon and tuna.

69
00:04:48,094 --> 00:04:53,627
Then let’s order salmon and tuna.

70
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:57,884
Does it come with wasabi?

71
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:02,540
I’m not good with spicy stuff.

72
00:05:02,563 --> 00:05:08,667
You can select ‘no wasabi’ on the touchscreen.

73
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:12,357
Great!

74
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:16,513
I’d like salmon without wasabi, please.

75
00:05:16,536 --> 00:05:21,003
Okay, I’ve pressed the button.

76
00:05:21,026 --> 00:05:27,359
The plates are different colors—do they have different prices?

77
00:05:27,382 --> 00:05:35,057
Yes. White plates are 100 yen, and red plates are 200 yen.

78
00:05:35,081 --> 00:05:38,947
That’s very clear!

79
00:05:38,970 --> 00:05:45,404
Oh, the salmon I ordered just arrived on the Shinkansen!

80
00:05:45,426 --> 00:05:50,304
Wow, the Shinkansen stopped!

81
00:05:50,328 --> 00:05:53,561
How cute!

82
00:05:53,584 --> 00:05:59,251
Grab the plate and press the button above, okay?

83
00:05:59,274 --> 00:06:02,941
Got it.

84
00:06:02,964 --> 00:06:06,664
It’s so pretty!

85
00:06:06,687 --> 00:06:10,987
Dip it in soy sauce and enjoy!

86
00:06:11,010 --> 00:06:13,676
Itadakimasu!

87
00:06:13,699 --> 00:06:18,878
The fish is so tender and delicious!

88
00:06:18,902 --> 00:06:22,637
Please eat a lot!

89
00:06:22,661 --> 00:06:28,927
There’s also sushi, but they have ice cream and cake too.

90
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:32,709
They have dessert too!

91
00:06:32,733 --> 00:06:37,006
I’d like to have ice cream later.

92
00:06:37,029 --> 00:06:39,963
Sounds good!

93
00:06:39,986 --> 00:06:47,019
After eating a lot, we’ll count the plates and pay the bill.

94
00:06:47,042 --> 00:06:50,175
Got it.

95
00:06:50,198 --> 00:06:55,231
Let’s enjoy eating lots of delicious sushi!

96
00:06:55,254 --> 00:06:59,253
Yes, let’s eat and have fun!

97
00:06:59,277 --> 00:07:00,777
Scene 3: Ordering at a Ramen Restaurant

98
00:07:00,777 --> 00:07:03,947
Excuse me.

99
00:07:03,971 --> 00:07:06,804
Welcome!

100
00:07:06,827 --> 00:07:10,937
Please take a seat at the counter.

101
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,902
Thank you.

102
00:07:13,926 --> 00:07:17,559
I bought a meal ticket.

103
00:07:17,582 --> 00:07:20,349
Excuse me.

104
00:07:20,372 --> 00:07:25,705
Yes, I’ll take your meal ticket.

105
00:07:25,728 --> 00:07:31,165
One soy sauce ramen and a dumpling set.

106
00:07:31,189 --> 00:07:33,977
Thank you.

107
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,878
How would you like your noodles?

108
00:07:37,902 --> 00:07:41,736
What noodle options do you have?

109
00:07:41,759 --> 00:07:48,792
We have firm noodles, regular noodles, and soft noodles.

110
00:07:48,815 --> 00:07:54,315
Since it's my first time, I'll go with regular noodles, please.

111
00:07:54,338 --> 00:07:57,638
Got it.

112
00:07:57,661 --> 00:08:00,728
Regular it is.

113
00:08:00,751 --> 00:08:05,784
Can I change the soup flavor too?

114
00:08:05,807 --> 00:08:08,341
Yes,

115
00:08:08,364 --> 00:08:15,242
We have rich, regular, and light flavors.

116
00:08:15,265 --> 00:08:20,044
I'll have the light flavor, please.

117
00:08:20,067 --> 00:08:23,367
Got it.

118
00:08:23,390 --> 00:08:27,290
Light soup it is.

119
00:08:27,314 --> 00:08:32,661
I'd also like to add an egg to the ramen.

120
00:08:32,684 --> 00:08:35,475
How much is it?

121
00:08:35,499 --> 00:08:40,732
An egg is 100 yen each.

122
00:08:40,755 --> 00:08:43,989
It's very delicious.

123
00:08:44,012 --> 00:08:48,881
Then, one egg, please.

124
00:08:48,904 --> 00:08:54,638
Here you go—100 yen, please.

125
00:08:54,661 --> 00:08:58,894
What’s on the table?

126
00:08:58,917 --> 00:09:02,866
That’s dumpling sauce.

127
00:09:02,890 --> 00:09:08,327
We have soy sauce, vinegar, and chili oil.

128
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:12,050
Is the chili oil spicy?

129
00:09:12,074 --> 00:09:19,457
Yes, it’s a little spicy, so just a tiny bit, please.

130
00:09:19,481 --> 00:09:22,458
Got it.

131
00:09:22,481 --> 00:09:26,782
Where’s the water?

132
00:09:26,806 --> 00:09:33,586
You can pour water from the pot in front of you into a glass.

133
00:09:33,610 --> 00:09:36,976
I’ll pour it myself.

134
00:09:36,999 --> 00:09:39,918
Thank you.

135
00:09:39,942 --> 00:09:43,495
Sorry to keep you waiting!

136
00:09:43,519 --> 00:09:48,786
Here’s your ramen with egg and soy sauce, and some dumplings!

137
00:09:48,809 --> 00:09:53,711
Wow, it smells amazing!

138
00:09:53,734 --> 00:09:59,282
It’s hot, so be careful while eating.

139
00:09:59,305 --> 00:10:02,239
Itadakimasu!

140
00:10:02,262 --> 00:10:07,632
The soup and noodles are both delicious!

141
00:10:07,655 --> 00:10:10,355
Thank you.

142
00:10:10,378 --> 00:10:13,945
Please enjoy your meal!

143
00:10:13,968 --> 00:10:15,468
Scene 4: Ordering at a Café

144
00:10:15,468 --> 00:10:18,135
Hello.

145
00:10:18,158 --> 00:10:21,108
Welcome!

146
00:10:21,131 --> 00:10:24,964
What would you like to order?

147
00:10:24,987 --> 00:10:30,864
I’d like a hot coffee and some cake.

148
00:10:30,888 --> 00:10:33,826
Thank you.

149
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:37,916
How about some cake?

150
00:10:37,939 --> 00:10:42,090
What kinds of cake do you have?

151
00:10:42,114 --> 00:10:49,814
We have cheesecake, chocolate cake, and matcha tart.

152
00:10:49,837 --> 00:10:54,109
Is the cheesecake sweet?

153
00:10:54,132 --> 00:11:00,038
It’s not too sweet and very delicious.

154
00:11:00,061 --> 00:11:04,636
Then, I’ll have the cheesecake, please.

155
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:08,494
Understood.

156
00:11:08,517 --> 00:11:13,750
I’ll make it a coffee and cake set for you.

157
00:11:13,773 --> 00:11:17,506
Is the set cheaper?

158
00:11:17,529 --> 00:11:20,162
Yes.

159
00:11:20,185 --> 00:11:25,689
The set is 50 yen cheaper.

160
00:11:25,713 --> 00:11:28,546
That’s great!

161
00:11:28,569 --> 00:11:31,803
I’ll take the set, please.

162
00:11:31,826 --> 00:11:36,292
What size would you like for the coffee?

163
00:11:36,315 --> 00:11:40,189
What sizes do you have?

164
00:11:40,213 --> 00:11:46,579
We have S, M, and L sizes.

165
00:11:46,602 --> 00:11:51,569
Then, M size, please.

166
00:11:51,592 --> 00:11:55,944
Would you like milk and sugar?

167
00:11:55,968 --> 00:12:02,559
No milk, but one sugar, please.

168
00:12:02,583 --> 00:12:05,486
Got it.

169
00:12:05,509 --> 00:12:09,251
One sugar, please.

170
00:12:09,274 --> 00:12:12,974
To eat here.

171
00:12:12,997 --> 00:12:16,331
Is there any available seat?

172
00:12:16,353 --> 00:12:19,087
Yes.

173
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:23,943
There’s an empty seat by the window in the back.

174
00:12:23,966 --> 00:12:27,806
I’ll take the window seat.

175
00:12:27,829 --> 00:12:30,896
Thank you.

176
00:12:30,919 --> 00:12:36,152
Your total is 750 yen.

177
00:12:36,175 --> 00:12:41,009
Can I pay by credit card?

178
00:12:41,032 --> 00:12:43,698
Yes.

179
00:12:43,721 --> 00:12:48,655
Please tap your card on this machine.

180
00:12:48,678 --> 00:12:51,744
I’ve tapped it.

181
00:12:51,767 --> 00:12:54,509
Thank you.

182
00:12:54,533 --> 00:12:59,692
Please take this numbered ticket and wait at your seat.

183
00:12:59,715 --> 00:13:03,388
Okay, got it.

184
00:13:03,412 --> 00:13:06,078
Thank you.

185
00:13:06,101 --> 00:13:11,235
I’ll bring your cake and coffee to your seat.

186
00:13:11,258 --> 00:13:12,758
Scene 5: Cheers at an Izakaya

187
00:13:12,758 --> 00:13:18,191
Thanks for your hard work today, Tanaka.

188
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:22,588
Thanks for your hard work, Yumi.

189
00:13:22,612 --> 00:13:26,519
Let’s go into the izakaya.

190
00:13:26,542 --> 00:13:29,084
Yes.

191
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:34,176
This place is lively and great, isn’t it?

192
00:13:34,199 --> 00:13:39,899
Shall we order drinks first?

193
00:13:39,922 --> 00:13:42,477
Sounds good!

194
00:13:42,501 --> 00:13:46,976
What would you like to drink, Tanaka?

195
00:13:46,999 --> 00:13:52,109
I’ll have a cold beer.

196
00:13:52,133 --> 00:13:55,833
What about you, Yumi?

197
00:13:55,856 --> 00:14:02,956
I’m not much of a drinker, so I’ll have oolong tea.

198
00:14:02,978 --> 00:14:06,445
Got it.

199
00:14:06,468 --> 00:14:13,801
Excuse me, one beer and one oolong tea, please.

200
00:14:13,824 --> 00:14:18,607
The drinks came quickly.

201
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:22,297
Well then, let’s make a toast!

202
00:14:22,321 --> 00:14:25,717
Thanks for your hard work.

203
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,528
Cheers!

204
00:14:28,551 --> 00:14:32,656
It’s cold and delicious!

205
00:14:32,679 --> 00:14:37,228
What would you like to order for food?

206
00:14:37,252 --> 00:14:42,886
I’d like yakitori and edamame.

207
00:14:42,909 --> 00:14:45,847
Sounds good!

208
00:14:45,870 --> 00:14:53,039
Yakitori comes in salt or tare flavor— which do you prefer?

209
00:14:53,063 --> 00:14:58,454
I prefer salt.

210
00:14:58,477 --> 00:15:02,744
Then let’s order yakitori with salt.

211
00:15:02,767 --> 00:15:07,085
They also have a sashimi set.

212
00:15:07,108 --> 00:15:10,775
Sashimi sounds good too.

213
00:15:10,798 --> 00:15:14,716
Shall we order it together?

214
00:15:14,739 --> 00:15:18,373
Yes, let’s order it.

215
00:15:18,396 --> 00:15:24,229
Is there anything you can’t eat, Yumi?

216
00:15:24,252 --> 00:15:30,886
I can’t eat shrimp, so I’ll avoid dishes with shrimp.

217
00:15:30,910 --> 00:15:34,043
Got it.

218
00:15:34,066 --> 00:15:38,341
I’ll choose a dish without shrimp.

219
00:15:38,364 --> 00:15:41,400
Thank you.

220
00:15:41,423 --> 00:15:46,018
Would you like to have a vegetable salad too?

221
00:15:46,041 --> 00:15:49,223
Sounds good!

222
00:15:49,247 --> 00:15:54,006
Let’s go with a tomato and tofu salad.

223
00:15:54,030 --> 00:15:57,068
That sounds great.

224
00:15:57,091 --> 00:16:00,125
Let’s order that too.

225
00:16:00,148 --> 00:16:04,814
Excuse me, we’d like to order.

226
00:16:04,837 --> 00:16:10,178
Thanks for ordering, Tanaka.

227
00:16:10,202 --> 00:16:16,389
No problem! Let’s eat and talk a lot.

228
00:16:16,413 --> 00:16:21,748
Yes, let’s enjoy lots of delicious food!

229
00:16:21,771 --> 00:16:27,087
While we wait for the food, let’s have some edamame.

230
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:28,610
Scene 6: How to Choose Pasta and Pizza

231
00:16:28,610 --> 00:16:35,982
Kenji, this Italian restaurant is so beautiful!

232
00:16:36,006 --> 00:16:40,039
It sure is, Emi.

233
00:16:40,062 --> 00:16:46,429
They’re famous here for their pasta and pizza!

234
00:16:46,452 --> 00:16:51,285
There are so many options on the menu.

235
00:16:51,308 --> 00:16:54,742
What do you want to order?

236
00:16:54,765 --> 00:17:02,065
Let’s get one pasta and one pizza to share between us.

237
00:17:02,088 --> 00:17:05,468
That sounds great!

238
00:17:05,491 --> 00:17:12,191
We can enjoy both pasta and pizza!

239
00:17:12,214 --> 00:17:16,314
Which pasta do you want?

240
00:17:16,337 --> 00:17:23,606
There’s tomato pasta and creamy pasta.

241
00:17:23,630 --> 00:17:28,663
I love tomato pasta.

242
00:17:28,686 --> 00:17:35,236
Then let’s go with tomato and bacon pasta!

243
00:17:35,259 --> 00:17:39,326
What about the pizza?

244
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:44,649
I’d love a cheese and tomato pizza.

245
00:17:44,672 --> 00:17:48,805
That’s a Margherita pizza!

246
00:17:48,828 --> 00:17:53,262
It’s really popular here.

247
00:17:53,285 --> 00:17:57,985
What size pizza do you want?

248
00:17:58,008 --> 00:18:03,474
An M size should be perfect.

249
00:18:03,497 --> 00:18:09,064
Okay, let’s go with M size.

250
00:18:09,087 --> 00:18:14,187
Let’s ask for two small plates too.

251
00:18:14,210 --> 00:18:19,550
Yeah, let’s ask the waiter.

252
00:18:19,573 --> 00:18:23,807
What would you like to drink?

253
00:18:23,830 --> 00:18:29,196
I’ll have an iced tea.

254
00:18:29,219 --> 00:18:34,086
I’ll go with orange juice.

255
00:18:34,109 --> 00:18:39,479
Excuse me, we’d like to order!

256
00:18:39,502 --> 00:18:44,940
Thanks for ordering, Kenji.

257
00:18:44,964 --> 00:18:52,512
No problem. Oh, our food’s here!

258
00:18:52,535 --> 00:18:59,840
Wow, the pizza’s so hot and loaded with cheese!

259
00:18:59,863 --> 00:19:05,730
Here, help yourself to some on your plate.

260
00:19:05,753 --> 00:19:08,700
Let’s dig in!

261
00:19:08,724 --> 00:19:13,357
The cheese is so delicious!

262
00:19:13,380 --> 00:19:20,514
The pasta’s warm too—go ahead and eat.

263
00:19:20,537 --> 00:19:26,270
The tomato pasta is really tasty!

264
00:19:26,293 --> 00:19:33,326
After the meal, how about dessert?

265
00:19:33,349 --> 00:19:36,516
Sounds good!

266
00:19:36,539 --> 00:19:40,688
Let’s get tiramisu together!

267
00:19:40,712 --> 00:19:46,012
Yeah, let’s order tiramisu too!

268
00:19:46,035 --> 00:19:47,535
Scene 7: Ordering Conversation Practice

269
00:19:47,535 --> 00:19:50,768
Excuse me.

270
00:19:50,791 --> 00:19:54,529
Yes, welcome!

271
00:19:54,553 --> 00:19:59,386
Please follow me to this table.

272
00:19:59,409 --> 00:20:02,326
Thank you.

273
